; AX3040 conflates two shapes, and only one of them is unsound.
;
; `347-result-only-tyvar.ax` is the unsound one: a body that CASTS a
; machine word out through a result type the caller picks. This file is
; the other one, and it is a CORRECT PROGRAM.
;
; `panic` promises `forall a. String -> a`. That signature is inhabited
; only by non-termination - `explain AX3040` says so in those words -
; and `panic` is exactly that inhabitant: every path through it reaches
; `exit`, so it never returns and never produces a value of the type
; the caller named. Nothing is coerced, nothing is dereferenced, and no
; caller can observe a wrong answer, because no caller is resumed.
;
; It is a shape a real program wants. A checked accessor, an assertion,
; an unrecoverable configuration error - each is a function whose type
; is honestly `forall a`, called in a position that expects an `Int` or
; a `String` and simply never gets there.
;
; MEASURED 2026-08-24, both paths, on the compiler that reports this:
;
;     (pick 7)        -> exits 7,  `panic` never entered
;     (pick (- 0 1))  -> writes "negative" to fd 2 and exits 70
;
; so the program is right on the path that returns AND on the path that
; does not.
;
; WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS. `tests/diagnostics/severity.policy` used to
; keep AX3040 a warning because promoting it needed a migration of
; fourteen declarations. That migration finished on 2026-08-23, and a
; sweep of 479 files on 2026-08-24 found exactly one AX3040 in the whole
; tree - 347's, constructed on purpose. So the recorded blocker was
; gone, and promoting the code looked free.
;
; It is not free, and this file is why: promotion would refuse the
; program below, and the help text would tell its author to tag a
; diverging function `;@axiom:raw`. That tag means "a raw word read
; whose meaning the type system does not model", which this is not, and
; its whole value is that the layer it enumerates is exact. A check
; whose suggested fix makes the program less correct is the wrong
; check.
;
; What promotion needs first is a way to tell divergence from a cast: a
; spelling for "does not return", or a walk proving every path exits.
; Until one exists, this file is the control that keeps the shape
; visible - if it ever stops drawing AX3040, something learned the
; difference and `severity.policy` should be re-read.
;
; `sound` is the control in the other direction and must stay silent:
; `a` appears in a PARAMETER, so the caller supplies a value of it and
; the choice is witnessed by the argument.
(import IO)

(:: panic (-> String a))

(fn (panic msg)
  {
    (writeStr 2 msg)
    (cast a (exit 70))
  }
)

(:: sound (-> a a))

(fn (sound x) x)

(:: pick (-> Int Int))

(fn (pick n)
  (if (< n 0)
    (panic "negative\n")
    n
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (pick 7))
